---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { latest, fmtUtc } from '../lib/data';
import { INPUT_VB, OUTPUT_VB } from '../lib/calc.mjs';
const ld = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'TechArticle', headline: 'How the network log is recorded', dateModified: '2026-10-15', datePublished: '2026-10-15',
  author: { '@id': 'https://dailycryptonews.online/#org' }, publisher: { '@id': 'https://dailycryptonews.online/#org' }, mainEntityOfPage: 'https://dailycryptonews.online/methodology/',
}];
---
<Page title="Methodology: How the Bitcoin & Ethereum Network Log Works" description="Where every number in the Daily Crypto News log comes from: mempool.space, Binance spot prices and Ethereum JSON-RPC, plus our formulas and stale-data rules." path="/methodology/" h1="How the network log is recorded" mark="Methodology" updated="2026-10-15" ld={ld}
  answer="Each reading pulls fee estimates, mempool size, difficulty and hashrate from mempool.space, spot prices from Binance’s public market data, and Ethereum fee history from a public JSON-RPC node. We compute dollar costs with fixed formulas, keep the last good data on failures and never backfill.">
  <h2 id="sources">Data sources</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Source</th><th>Latest snapshot</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Recommended fee rates, mempool, difficulty, hashrate, block height</td><td><a href="https://mempool.space/docs/api/rest">mempool.space REST API</a></td><td>{fmtUtc(latest.btc.asOf)}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>BTC and ETH price (USDT pairs as a USD proxy)</td><td><a href="https://developers.binance.com/docs/binance-spot-api-docs/rest-api/market-data-endpoints">Binance spot public market data</a></td><td>{latest.prices ? fmtUtc(latest.prices.asOf) : 'unavailable'}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ethereum base fee, priority tips, block fullness</td><td><a href="https://ethereum.org/en/developers/docs/apis/json-rpc/">eth_feeHistory</a> via the public endpoint ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com</td><td>{latest.eth ? fmtUtc(latest.eth.asOf) : 'unavailable'}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>USDT is a stablecoin that usually trades close to one US dollar but is not identical to it; dollar figures are therefore approximations. We do not use exchange prices to promote any exchange, and we carry no exchange affiliate links.</p>

  <h2 id="schedule">When readings are taken</h2>
  <p>A refresh script runs on a schedule on our own machine, fetches every source, and rebuilds the static site. Each reading is stored with its own timestamp in UTC. A day’s archive page is created only when at least one reading was actually recorded that day; the log began on 15 October 2026 and contains nothing before then.</p>

  <h2 id="stale">Failures and stale data</h2>
  <p>If a source fails, we keep the last good values for that source and print its real timestamp with a “stale” warning. We never interpolate, estimate missing readings or substitute another source silently. Any reading older than six hours at build time is flagged as stale on the page.</p>

  <h2 id="vsize">Transaction size formulas</h2>
  <p>Virtual size = 10 vB overhead + inputs + outputs, plus 0.5 vB when any input carries witness data, rounded up (BIP 141 weight ÷ 4). Standard sizes used:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Input (vB)</th><th>Output (vB)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Legacy P2PKH</td><td>{INPUT_VB.p2pkh}</td><td>{OUTPUT_VB.p2pkh}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Nested SegWit P2SH-P2WPKH</td><td>{INPUT_VB['p2sh-p2wpkh']}</td><td>{OUTPUT_VB.p2sh} (P2SH)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Native SegWit P2WPKH</td><td>{INPUT_VB.p2wpkh}</td><td>{OUTPUT_VB.p2wpkh}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Taproot P2TR (key path)</td><td>{INPUT_VB.p2tr}</td><td>{OUTPUT_VB.p2tr}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Fee (sats) = ceil(size × rate). USD = sats ÷ 100,000,000 × BTC price. An Ethereum transfer = 21,000 gas × (latest base fee + median 50th-percentile tip over the last 20 blocks).</p>

  <h2 id="sea-state">Sea-state bands</h2>
  <p>Backlog in blocks = total pending virtual size ÷ 1,000,000 vB. Bands: Calm under 1; Light swell 1–3; Choppy 3–10; Rough 10–30; Storm 30 or more. These bands are our reading aid, not an industry standard, and do not by themselves predict the fee you need.</p>

  <h2 id="halving">Countdown estimates</h2>
  <p>Halving dates use the protocol target of 600 seconds per block. Difficulty projections are taken from mempool.space and assume the current epoch’s average block time continues.</p>

  <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
  <p>If you find an error, email <a href="/contact/">contact@dailycryptonews.online</a>. Corrections to guides are dated in the guide’s “last reviewed” line. Recorded readings are not edited after the fact; if a source later revises a value, the log keeps what was observed. See also <a href="/about/">about us</a> and today’s <a href="/">network log</a>.</p>
</Page>
